As part of my on going balance adjustments that I've been making to my
own version of nethack, I've had an idea for tweaking the skill
system. I think it's a good idea, but before I implement it I'd like
to run it past the experts on this board to make sure there aren't
serious problems that I haven't thought of.

So, onto the idea. First let me describe what I see as a problem in
the current skills system.

There are heaps of different weapon types in the game, and most of
them are associated with their own special weapon skill. This is cool
and somewhat realistic, but the problem for gameplay is that since we
have a limited number of skill slots to use, the lesser weapon types
get completely shunned. For example, advancing in short swords is just
a trap. It's essentially just a waste of skill points on a weapon type
that has no future.

At first I thought it might be better to just eliminate a bunch of
weapon skills from the game, and roll the orphaned weapons into the
remaining skills. But this could give rise to balance problems with
certain roles which can currently reach expert in the lesser weapons
but are restricted in the stronger weapons. So I didn't act on this
idea.

Now I think I've got a better idea. Instead of completely eliminating
skills, I'd like to tie certain skills together. The way it would work
is that each weapon skill would require practice to enhance, just as
they do in the current system, but certain skills would share their
skill points. So for example, if a character enhances their 'daggers'
skill to expert, they will then be able to enhance 'knives' to expert
as well with no cost of skill points. Simply practicing with a knife
will automatically advance the knives skill when the required levels
of practice have been reached, with no cost in the number of skill
points. (However, there will be no discount in the amount of practice
required for enhancing these related skills.)

The point is that if weak skills are partnered with stronger skills in
this way, then there would be less counter-incentive to shun the
weaker weapons.

Here are some of the related skill pairs I have in mind.
dagger & knife
spear & javelin
dart & shuriken
short sword & long sword
scimitar & saber

after than it starts to get a bit tricky... it would be nice to have
everything in pairs, but some weapons don't really pair very well, and
others seem more suitable for triplets or something.

club & mace & morning star ?
polearm & lance ?
quarterstaff & trident ??
bow & crossbow & sling ?
axe & pickaxe ?
hammer and flail ?=BF
boomerang with dart & shuriken ?
unicorn horn & whip (lolwut?)

yeah... so maybe it isn't all completely smooth sailing. There are
some pairings that seem natural and balanced, but others that seem
forced and arbitrary. In any case, I'd like to know what people think
of the basic idea; and I'd welcome advice as to how to group the
skills if the idea seems sound. (Also, let me know if I haven't
explained the idea clearly.)


